**Item 03 is done and marked `[x]`; the gate passes.** The expansion family's exact half now runs by SAT with checked DRAT proofs, and the record says where that works and where it does not.

**What was built**
- `exact_sat` and `expansion_cnf` in `learning/obstruction_expansion.py`: the "no `t`-set has `|N[C]| ≤ b`" decision as a canonical CNF with my own full totalizer under a written contract, CaDiCaL through pysat with proof logging, a conflict budget and a wall deadline enforced by a forked child, drat-trim on every UNSAT, a certificate JSON per proved level. Stages `sat` and `sat-tables`.
- `paper1/obstruction_check.py check-expansion`: an independent checker with its own reader, graph, totalizer from the contract, hash comparison and drat-trim on the regenerated CNF. It imports nothing from the four project packages. A test pins its docstring to the contract text.
- Six new tests (encoding agrees with enumeration on 100 graphs at every `(t, b)`; a genuine certificate verifies and three kinds of damage are rejected; checker and search hashes agree on 20 instances; committed-file guards).

**What the run found** (6 core-hour cap, 144 of 148 bracketed targets reached)
- The bracket closed on 72 targets. Family E's duality gap is now exact on 264 of the 338, up from 193.
- Every bracket at 30 to 60 customers closed in seconds. At 75 it closed on 2 of 13, at 76 to 100 on 1 of 41, at 101 to 134 on none.
- The exact floor closes 12 of the 338 (7 before) and beats the harness reference on 98 (87 before). Six of the 338 stay open with a bracket, all dense 100 to 125 customer instances.
- On the SCOOP instance with 79 customers, SAT answers lowered the ceiling to 7, equal to the floor, against an optimum of 13: the family's gap there is exactly 6.
- All 158 certificates on disk verify through the independent checker. The harness validity stage reports the SAT floor above no optimum on all 6,376 corpus instances.

**Kill verdict: met.** SAT settled the argmax level on 70 of the 145 bracketed instances of the 338 (48.3%, below the 50% criterion). The record states that Harper exact is out of reach by SAT above cap 12 at 75 customers and beyond on the Chu & Stuckey graphs, with the boundary at `n ≈ 60–75` at the argmax levels, and fully in reach to 60.

**Two things to know**
- The gzipped proofs total 1.3 GB, so I added one `.gitignore` rule for `*.drat.gz` under the obstruction scratch tree. They stay on disk and regenerate from the stage's command; every certificate JSON keeps the proof's hash and size. Said so in the report and PROGRESS.
- One deviation from the item's text, recorded in the report: levels whose value equals the floor are not asked, since they can move neither half of the bracket.

Compute was about 6.2 core-hours against the item's 6, the overrun being the independent re-check of every certificate. Nothing was committed; the driver commits. Next is item 04, family M.

